=== FINDINGS
1. Row arithmetic (Verified by measurement at 1280×720): figure 264→520 px sits inside rows 3–5 (≈389 px) — it never stretched them. The +~50 px that broke TC-HERO-08/09 came from the grading note moving under the ledger (spec §4 ledgerRow 1fr). Fixed with a `max-height: 860px` rhythm block placed AFTER the base rules (ledgerRow/actions margin → --space-3, availability → --space-2): action bottom 733→697 px, hero 813→761 px.
2. The pre-existing `@media (max-height: 860px)` block at the top of Hero.module.css is dead by source order for .name/.role/.statement/.ledger/.actions/.availability (the base rules set the same properties later and win): `.role` measures margin-top 17.28 px, not the 8 px it declares. Left as-is (changing it re-sizes the h1 at short viewports — outside this cycle); noted for the owner. [Verified]
3. RM-4 (Hero) initially failed because the pause button declared colour transitions by default and is absent under reduced motion (TC-HERO-14 requires count 0) — the check keys on DOM identity. Fixed by giving the toggle no colour transition. [Verified]
4. figcaption omitted (spec marks it optional): at 1280×720 a two-line mono caption (+~44 px) would have re-broken the fold. [Inferred from finding 1]
5. Portrait boxes measured: 390→88×88 stamp (no <video>, no button) · 834→176×220 · 1280→205×256 · 1440→230×288; filter grayscale(1) contrast(1.04) on the wrapper at every width; loop playing at opacity 1 at ≥834 with src /assets/my-hero-avatar.mp4 assigned by the gate. [Verified]
6. `pauses when the MiniVic panel speaks` uses useAvatarSpeaking() only — the context exposes `speaking`, not "panel open". [Verified — lib/avatarContext.tsx]
7. components/site/HeroAvatar.tsx deleted; remaining mentions are comments only (lib/voiceoverController.ts:14, lib/avatarContext.tsx:7,43, tests/overhaul/avatar.spec.ts:8, tests/e2e/clone-voice.spec.ts:8) — no importer. [Verified — grep]
